quick:
  - label: Events Calendar
    note: Month by month, with organizer links
    href: /events/
  - label: Business Directory
    note: Eat, shop and local services
    href: /eat-shop/
  - label: Parks & Trails
    note: Whistle Stop Park and the regional trail
    href: /explore/#outdoors
  - label: Community Organizations
    note: Groups to join and who runs what
    href: /community/
  - label: Resident Resources
    note: County services, water, fire, schools
    href: /community/#resources
  - label: 2026 Incorporation Election
    note: Ballot questions and official resources
    href: /civic/incorporation-election/
categories:
  - Coffee & Bakery
  - Restaurants & Bars
  - Grocery & Provisions
  - Home & Garden
  - Gifts & Books
  - Arts & Makers
  - Health & Wellness
  - Services
outdoors:
  - label: Whistle Stop Park
    body: The caboose, open lawn and the summer concert ground, at the edge of Old Town.
  - label: Regional trail
    body: The Boulder-to-Longmont trail corridor runs past the community and links to quiet county roads.
  - label: Managed by
    body: Boulder County Parks & Open Space sets trail surfaces, closures and dog rules here.
resources:
  - what: Roads, permits and open space
    who: Boulder County
    href: https://bouldercounty.gov/
  - what: Drinking water
    who: Left Hand Water
    href: https://lefthandwater.org/
  - what: Fire and rescue
    who: Mountain View
    href: https://www.mvfpd.org/
  - what: Schools
    who: St. Vrain Valley
    href: https://www.svvsd.org/
facts:
  - label: The name
    text: Niwot is named for Chief Niwot of the Southern Arapaho. The name is carried by the creek, the water district and the community.
  - label: The grid
    text: The street plan follows the 1875 town plat, laid out along the railroad rather than the county road grid that came later.
  - label: The edge
    text: Farmland begins immediately east of the storefronts. The walk from brick to open field takes about four minutes.
